 "teaches": [
  "A hero plus chart that survives the small sizes: every length is an expression of windowWidth() and windowHeight(), and the same tree stacks or goes side by side through spacer lengths",
  "Priority when short: first the stats, then the header, then the axis labels. The chart always stays and takes what is left",
  "One list from the host: the total and the peak are arraySum and arrayMax of the exported array, so they can never disagree with the chart",
  "The axis is a row of texts under the chart, not xLabels, so it can be dropped by visibility at run time; xLabels are fixed when the document is built",
  "BigNumber's own description says the value and change to a screen reader. Do not pass label unless you repeat them",
  "Swap the chart: BarChart with fill true takes the same array, and any canvas fits the same box"
 ],
 "snippets": [
  {
   "pointer": "/root/2",
   "shows": "layout.stack",
   "note": "the whole widget: header, then hero, chart and stats placed by spacer lengths in one box"
  },
  {
   "pointer": "/resources/variables/wide",
   "shows": "expr.system",
   "note": "stacked or side by side; hasStats, hasHead and hasAxis next to it drop the parts"
  },
  {
